            {
              "id": "2921bb56-8b1e-3c7b-aaa3-83670dd0dde6",
              "name": "Unicode Transformations Mismanagement Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nUnicode Transformations Mismanagement Vulnerability in Java refers to the improper handling of Unicode characters during transformations, such as converting a string to lower case or upper case. This can lead to security vulnerabilities, as it can allow an attacker to bypass security checks that are case-sensitive.\n\nIn the provided code example, the vulnerability arises when the `toLowerCase()` method is used on the `username` string. This method is locale-sensitive, meaning it can behave differently depending on the user's locale. For example, in the Turkish locale, the uppercase 'I' character is converted to a lowercase 'ı' (dotless i), not 'i'. If a security check is expecting the latter, it could be bypassed.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should use the `toLowerCase(Locale.English)` or `toUpperCase(Locale.English)` methods instead of the locale-sensitive versions. This ensures that the transformations are consistent regardless of the user's locale.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere's how you can fix the provided code example:\n\n```java\nimport java.util.Locale;\n\n// ...\n\nString lowerCasedUsername = username.toLowerCase(Locale.ENGLISH);\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code example does not require any additional library dependencies to execute properly.\n\n## OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP - Insecure Direct Object References](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A5_2017-Broken_Access_Control)\n- [OWASP - Unvalidated Redirects and Forwards](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A10_2017-Insufficient_Logging%2526Monitoring)\n\n## Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-200: Information Exposure](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html)\n- [CWE-807: Reliance on Untrusted Inputs in a Security Decision](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/807.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-200",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-807",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/807.html"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "FAIL",
