              "id": "4045512e-144c-32a5-8c3a-66f2a0a5bf2d",
              "name": "Unicode Transformations Mismanagement Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nUnicode Transformations Mismanagement Vulnerability in Java refers to the improper handling of Unicode transformations, which can lead to various security issues such as information leakage, data corruption, and denial of service. This vulnerability arises when a program does not properly handle Unicode sequences, which can be exploited by an attacker to bypass security controls, manipulate data, or cause the application to crash.\n\nIn the provided code snippet, the vulnerability is not directly related to Unicode transformations. However, the code is vulnerable to tampering as it uses a case-insensitive comparison to check if the request has been tampered with. An attacker could potentially manipulate the `paramValue` to bypass this check.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to use secure coding practices and libraries that properly handle Unicode transformations. Additionally, avoid using case-insensitive comparisons for security checks. Instead, use cryptographic methods to ensure the integrity of data.\n\n## Code Fix Recommendation\n\nInstead of using a case-insensitive comparison, consider using a secure hash function to verify the integrity of `paramValue`. Here is an example using SHA-256:\n\n```java\nimport java.security.MessageDigest;\nimport java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;\nimport java.math.BigInteger;\n\n// ...\n\nString originalValue = \"Requests are tampered easily\";\nMessageDigest digest = MessageDigest.getInstance(\"SHA-256\");\nbyte[] hash = digest.digest(originalValue.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));\nString hashedValue = String.format(\"%064x\", new BigInteger(1, hash));\n\nif (hashedValue.equals(paramValue)) {\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- Java SE Development Kit (JDK) 8 or later\n\n## OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\n- [OWASP Java Security](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A3_2017-Sensitive_Data_Exposure)\n\n## Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-20: Improper Input Validation](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html)\n- [CWE-707: Improper Neutralization](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/707.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
