              "id": "54f1696d-3f1d-317f-871b-fd9e40380ec4",
              "name": "Spring Endpoint Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Spring Endpoint Vulnerability\" is a type of Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability that occurs when an application includes untrusted data in a new web page without proper validation or escaping, or updates an existing web page with user-supplied data using a browser API that can create HTML or JavaScript. XSS allows attackers to execute scripts in the victim's browser which can hijack user sessions, deface web sites, or redirect the user to malicious sites.\n\nIn the provided Java code, the vulnerability lies in the fact that user-supplied data (`commentStr`) is being parsed and added to a list of comments without any form of sanitization or encoding. This data is then returned in the response, potentially leading to a Stored XSS attack if `commentStr` contains malicious scripts.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. Use the latest version of your libraries and frameworks as they usually come with security improvements.\n2. Always validate and sanitize user inputs to ensure they do not contain malicious scripts.\n3. Use context-specific output encoding when inserting user-supplied data into HTML to prevent XSS attacks.\n4. Use Content Security Policy (CSP) to mitigate the impact of any potential XSS vulnerabilities.\n\n## Source Code Fix\n\nA simple fix would be to sanitize the `commentStr` before parsing it:\n\n```java\nimport org.owasp.encoder.Encode;\n// ...\nComment comment = parseJson(Encode.forHtmlContent(commentStr));\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- Spring Framework\n- Java Time API\n- OWASP Java Encoder library for the fix\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS (Cross Site Scripting) Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Java Encoder library](https://owasp.org/www-project-java-encoder/)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
