              "id": "fbdb57c9-1a2b-300c-bb3e-1d0e481f1baa",
              "name": "Unicode Transformation Mismanagement Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nUnicode Transformation Mismanagement Vulnerability in Java refers to the improper handling of Unicode characters by an application. This can lead to a variety of security issues, including bypassing input validation checks, cross-site scripting (XSS), and SQL injection attacks. In the provided code sink, the vulnerability arises from the use of the `toUpperCase()` method, which can behave differently depending on the user's locale. For example, in the Turkish locale, the lowercase 'i' is converted to 'İ' (U+0130) instead of 'I'. This can lead to unexpected results and potential security issues.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should use the `toUpperCase(Locale.ENGLISH)` or `toLowerCase(Locale.ENGLISH)` methods instead of the default `toUpperCase()` or `toLowerCase()` methods. This ensures that the transformation is consistent regardless of the user's locale.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is the fixed version of the provided code sink:\n\n```java\n.equals(modulus.toUpperCase(Locale.ENGLISH)));\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code sink does not require any additional library dependencies to execute properly.\n\n## OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP - Insecure Direct Object References](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A5_2017-Broken_Access_Control)\n- [OWASP - Unvalidated Redirects and Forwards](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A10_2017-Insufficient_Logging%2526Monitoring)\n\n## Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-178: Improper Handling of Case Sensitivity](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/178.html)\n- [CWE-200: Information Exposure](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html)\n\nPlease note that all the provided links are active and accessible by anonymous users."
              },
